# 1. Static Review of Terms & Conditions

**Document selected:** Sample Terms & Conditions of a food-delivery app

Static testing means reviewing a document without actually executing the application. I read the terms and looked for statements that could be difficult for a normal user to understand.

| No. | Unclear / Ambiguous Statement                            | Why It Could Confuse Users                                                                  |
| --- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1   | “We may modify the services from time to time.”          | It does not clearly explain what type of changes can be made or how users will be informed. |
| 2   | “Additional charges may apply in certain circumstances.” | The user may not know what these circumstances are or how much the charges could be.        |
| 3   | “Offers are subject to applicable conditions.”           | The actual conditions are not mentioned clearly in the statement.                           |
| 4   | “We reserve the right to suspend your account.”          | It does not clearly explain what actions can result in account suspension.                  |
| 5   | “Delivery times are only estimates.”                     | Users may not understand how much the actual delivery time can vary.                        |

### Conclusion

The main issue I found during the static review is that legal documents often use broad terms such as **“certain circumstances,” “applicable conditions,” and “from time to time.”** These statements may be legally useful, but they can be confusing for ordinary users. They could be made clearer by using specific examples and simpler language.

